WEBVTT

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:01.751
Hi.

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:06.381
This guy says, "Hello,"
I want to kill myself.

00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:08.299
You okay, sweetie?

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:10.552
I just feel like
someone reached down my throat

00:00:10.593 --> 00:00:13.388
grabbed my small intestine,
pulled it out of my mouth

00:00:13.388 --> 00:00:14.889
and tied it around my neck.

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:16.474
Cookie?

00:00:18.268 --> 00:00:19.894
Carol moved her stuff out today.

00:00:19.936 --> 00:00:20.895
(all)
Ohh.

00:00:20.895 --> 00:00:23.023
- Let me get you some coffee.
- Thanks.

00:00:25.942 --> 00:00:27.527
Oh, ugh.

00:00:27.569 --> 00:00:32.115
Uh-oh, no. No, don't.
Stop cleansing my aura.

00:00:32.406 --> 00:00:34.868
Don't. Just leave
my aura alone, okay?

00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:38.246
I'll be fine, alright?
Really, everyone

00:00:38.246 --> 00:00:39.414
I hope she'll be very happy.

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:40.915
- No, you don't
- No, I don't.

00:00:40.915 --> 00:00:42.751
To hell with her, she left me!

00:00:43.918 --> 00:00:46.337
And you never knew
she was a lesbian.

00:00:50.258 --> 00:00:51.968
No, okay?

00:00:52.427 --> 00:00:55.430
Why does everyone
keep fixating on that?

00:00:56.765 --> 00:00:59.517
She didn't know,
how should I know?

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.897
Sometimes,
I wish I was a lesbian.

00:01:05.774 --> 00:01:08.109
Did I say that out loud?

00:01:09.652 --> 00:01:13.656
Alright, Ross, look, you're
feeling a lot of pain right now.

00:01:13.907 --> 00:01:16.451
You're angry.
You're hurting.

00:01:16.618 --> 00:01:18.787
Can I tell you
what the answer is?

00:01:18.995 --> 00:01:20.622
Strip joints!

00:01:22.457 --> 00:01:24.793
Come on, you're single.
Have some hormones..

00:01:24.793 --> 00:01:26.920
But I don't want
to be single, okay?

00:01:27.212 --> 00:01:30.465
I just, I just,
I just want to be married again.

00:01:34.552 --> 00:01:37.013
And I just
won a million dollars.

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:39.724
Rachel?

00:01:39.974 --> 00:01:42.811
[gasps]
Oh, God, Monica, hi. Thank god.

00:01:43.144 --> 00:01:44.854
I just went to your building
and you weren't there.

00:01:44.854 --> 00:01:47.482
And then this guy with a big
hammer said you might be here

00:01:47.482 --> 00:01:48.942
and you are. You are.

00:01:48.983 --> 00:01:50.693
Can I get you some coffee?

00:01:50.693 --> 00:01:52.695
Decaf.

00:01:53.071 --> 00:01:57.033
Okay, everybody this is Rachel,
another Lincoln High survivor.

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:58.034
This-this is everybody.

00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.452
This is Chandler, and Phoebe

00:01:59.494 --> 00:02:00.662
and Joey.

00:02:00.703 --> 00:02:02.330
And you remember
my brother, Ross?

00:02:02.372 --> 00:02:03.873
- Sure! Hi.
- Hey.

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:15.760
So you want to tell us now,
or are we waiting

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:17.512
for four wet bridesmaids?

00:02:19.222 --> 00:02:21.057
Oh, God! Well..

00:02:21.224 --> 00:02:24.102
...it started about a half-hour
before the wedding.

00:02:24.435 --> 00:02:26.896
I was in this room where
we were keeping all the presents

00:02:26.896 --> 00:02:29.107
And I was looking
at this gravy boat.

00:02:29.107 --> 00:02:32.277
This really
gorgeous Limoges gravy boat.

00:02:32.527 --> 00:02:34.404
When all of sudden..
Sweet N' Low?

00:02:34.487 --> 00:02:36.489
I realized

00:02:36.865 --> 00:02:38.449
I realized I was
more turned on

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.702
by this gravy boat
than by Barry.

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.787
And then I got
really freaked out.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:44.038
And that's when it hit me

00:02:44.038 --> 00:02:46.749
how much Barry
looks Mr. Potato Head.

00:02:47.125 --> 00:02:50.253
You know, I mean, I always
knew he looked familiar, but..

00:02:52.755 --> 00:02:55.466
Anyway, I just had
to get out of there

00:02:55.466 --> 00:02:57.510
and I started wondering
"Why am I doing this?"

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.971
and "Who am I doing this for?"

00:03:00.221 --> 00:03:02.056
So, anyway,
I just didn't know where to go

00:03:02.056 --> 00:03:04.392
and I know that you and I
have kind of drifted apart

00:03:04.392 --> 00:03:07.937
but you're the only person I
knew who lived here in the city.

00:03:07.937 --> 00:03:09.731
Who wasn't
invited to the wedding.

00:03:09.772 --> 00:03:12.734
Oh, I was kind of hoping
that wouldn't be an issue.

00:03:15.069 --> 00:03:17.572
["Star spangled banner"
instrumental]

00:03:19.574 --> 00:03:21.910
Well, that's it.

00:03:21.993 --> 00:03:23.661
- You gonna crash on the couch?
- No.

00:03:23.745 --> 00:03:25.413
No, I gotta
go home, sometime.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:26.748
Alright.
You gonna be okay?

00:03:26.748 --> 00:03:29.167
- Yeah.
- Goodnight.

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:31.836
Hey, Mon, look what I just
found on the floor.

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:33.379
[chuckles]

00:03:33.421 --> 00:03:34.923
What?

00:03:35.006 --> 00:03:36.925
That's Paul's watch.

00:03:37.008 --> 00:03:39.052
Now, you just, put it back
where you found it.

00:03:40.428 --> 00:03:43.848
Oh, boy. Alright.
Goodnight, everybody.

00:03:43.932 --> 00:03:45.225
- Goodnight.
- Goodnight.

00:03:45.266 --> 00:03:46.434
[thud]

00:03:51.731 --> 00:03:53.733
[chuckling]

00:03:53.775 --> 00:03:55.735
- Hmm.
- 'Hmm.'

00:03:55.777 --> 00:03:57.111
- Hmm. Oh, no.
- Oh, sorry.

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:58.571
- Oh, no, no. Go. Go-go.
- No, have it, really.

00:03:58.613 --> 00:03:59.781
- I don't want.
- Split it?

00:03:59.781 --> 00:04:01.115
- Okay.
- Okay.

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:02.867
[chuckles]

00:04:04.285 --> 00:04:05.453
Thanks.

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:07.622
You probably didn't know this
but back in high school

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.624
I had a..

00:04:09.624 --> 00:04:11.376
...major crush on you.

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.128
I knew.

00:04:14.212 --> 00:04:15.463
You did? Oh.

00:04:15.463 --> 00:04:17.465
[scoffs]

00:04:17.589 --> 00:04:18.632
I always figured
you just thought

00:04:18.632 --> 00:04:21.301
I was Monica's
geeky older brother.

00:04:21.302 --> 00:04:22.971
- I did.
- Oh.

00:04:27.809 --> 00:04:29.811
Listen, do you think

00:04:29.811 --> 00:04:31.813
and try not to let
my intense vulnerability

00:04:31.896 --> 00:04:33.314
become any kind
of a factor here

00:04:35.149 --> 00:04:36.484
but you think
it would be okay

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.319
if I asked you out
sometime maybe?

00:04:40.488 --> 00:04:41.823
Yeah.

00:04:42.824 --> 00:04:44.158
Maybe.

00:04:45.326 --> 00:04:46.452
Okay.

00:04:51.666 --> 00:04:53.793
Okay, maybe I will.

00:04:54.335 --> 00:04:56.129
[laughing]

00:04:57.505 --> 00:04:59.841
- Alright. Goodnight.
- Goodnight.

00:05:03.011 --> 00:05:05.471
[door opens and closes]

00:05:13.521 --> 00:05:16.190
See ya.

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:17.191
Mm-hmm.

00:05:17.275 --> 00:05:18.109
Wait, wait.

00:05:18.192 --> 00:05:19.861
Hey, what's with you?

00:05:21.779 --> 00:05:23.823
I just grabbed a spoon.

00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:27.201
[instrumental music]

00:05:31.456 --> 00:05:33.207
Look , I'm sorry, guys,
I just don't wanna give them

00:05:33.291 --> 00:05:35.043
any more ammunition
than they already have.

00:05:35.126 --> 00:05:37.628
Yes, and we all know
how cruel a parent can be about

00:05:37.628 --> 00:05:40.131
the flatness
of a child's pillow.

00:05:41.215 --> 00:05:43.968
Monica, hi! Um..

00:05:44.052 --> 00:05:47.513
Monica, you're scaring me.

00:05:47.638 --> 00:05:50.808
I mean, you're like, you're all
chaotic and twirly, you know.

00:05:50.892 --> 00:05:53.019
And not-not in a good way.

00:05:54.812 --> 00:05:56.064
Yeah, calm down.

00:05:56.147 --> 00:05:57.982
You don't see Ross
getting all chaotic

00:05:58.066 --> 00:06:00.818
and twirly every time they come.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.987
That's because as far
as my parents are concerned

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:04.822
Ross can do no wrong.

00:06:04.822 --> 00:06:06.657
You see, he's the prince.

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:10.328
Apparently they had some big
ceremony before I was born.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:14.832
- Ew, ew, ew!
- What?

00:06:14.874 --> 00:06:18.211
Ugly naked guy
got a Thighmaster.

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:20.505
(in unison)
Ew!

00:06:21.839 --> 00:06:23.508
Has anybody seen
my engagement ring?

00:06:23.549 --> 00:06:25.843
Yeah, it's beautiful.

00:06:30.181 --> 00:06:33.518
Oh, God. Oh, God. Oh, God.

00:06:33.518 --> 00:06:35.353
No-no, don't touch that.

00:06:37.522 --> 00:06:39.899
Oh, like I wasn't dreading
tomorrow enough

00:06:40.024 --> 00:06:42.026
having to give it back to him..

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:43.528
Hi, Barry! Remember me?

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:45.196
I'm the girl in the veil
who stomped on your heart

00:06:45.196 --> 00:06:47.240
in front of your entire family!

00:06:47.365 --> 00:06:49.617
Oh, God and now I'm gonna
have to return the ring

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:53.871
without the ring,
which makes it so much harder.

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:56.207
Easy, Rach,
we'll find it.

00:06:56.207 --> 00:06:58.584
- Won't we?
- Oh, yeah.

00:07:01.379 --> 00:07:02.880
Alright, when did you
have it on last?

00:07:02.964 --> 00:07:05.466
Doy! Probably
right before she lost it.

00:07:07.802 --> 00:07:10.471
You don't get
a lot of doy these days.

00:07:12.223 --> 00:07:14.642
I know, I had it this morning

00:07:14.725 --> 00:07:18.396
and I know I had it when
I was in the kitchen with..

00:07:18.479 --> 00:07:20.231
Dinah?

00:07:22.733 --> 00:07:25.736
Oh, don't be mad.

00:07:25.736 --> 00:07:28.072
- You didn't.
- Oh, I'm sorry.

00:07:28.156 --> 00:07:30.575
I gave you one job!

00:07:31.909 --> 00:07:35.121
Oh, but look how straight
those noodles are.

00:07:35.246 --> 00:07:37.081
Now, Monica, you know
that's not how you look

00:07:37.165 --> 00:07:40.293
for an engagement ring
in a lasagna.

00:07:42.253 --> 00:07:45.006
I just can't do it.

00:07:45.089 --> 00:07:48.593
Boys? We're going in.

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:54.474
[knock on door]

00:07:57.435 --> 00:07:59.479
Hi.

00:07:59.604 --> 00:08:01.814
Wow. That is not a happy hi.

00:08:01.939 --> 00:08:03.608
Carol's pregnant.

00:08:03.608 --> 00:08:05.526
Ooh! I found it!

00:08:07.612 --> 00:08:10.865
W-w-what?

00:08:10.948 --> 00:08:12.325
Yeah.

00:08:13.284 --> 00:08:14.535
Do that for another two hours

00:08:14.619 --> 00:08:17.497
you might be where
I am right about now.

00:08:18.956 --> 00:08:22.168
Kinda puts that whole pillow
thing in perspective, huh, Mon?

00:08:24.295 --> 00:08:26.297
Well now, how how do you fit
into this whole thing?

00:08:26.297 --> 00:08:29.675
Well, Carol says she
and Susan want me to be involved

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:34.847
but if I'm not comfortable with
it, I don't have to be involved.

00:08:34.972 --> 00:08:36.974
Basically it's totally up to me.

00:08:37.058 --> 00:08:39.310
She is so great! I miss her.

00:08:43.898 --> 00:08:45.650
Well, what does she mean
by involved?

00:08:45.691 --> 00:08:48.694
I mean, presumably the biggest
part of your job is done.

00:08:50.655 --> 00:08:53.491
Anyway, they want me
to go down to this

00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:55.493
sonogram thing
with them tomorrow.

00:08:55.535 --> 00:08:57.745
- Wow.
- So what are you gonna do?

00:08:57.828 --> 00:08:59.580
I have no idea.

00:08:59.664 --> 00:09:02.667
No matter what I do, though,
I'm still gonna be a father.

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:04.669
[cutlery clanking]

00:09:13.511 --> 00:09:16.180
Well, this is still
ruined, right?

00:12:05.182 --> 00:12:06.475
No, no, no.

00:12:06.517 --> 00:12:08.185
They say it's the
same as the distance

00:12:08.185 --> 00:12:10.104
from the tip of a guy's thumb

00:12:10.187 --> 00:12:11.689
the the tip of his index finger.

00:12:18.195 --> 00:12:19.947
That's ridiculous.

00:12:21.365 --> 00:12:23.367
Can I use either thumb?

00:12:24.702 --> 00:12:26.620
Alright. Don't tell me.
Don't tell me.

00:12:28.038 --> 00:12:30.541
Decaf cappuccino for Joey.

00:12:33.002 --> 00:12:34.503
Coffee, black.

00:12:35.796 --> 00:12:37.298
Latte.

00:12:39.133 --> 00:12:40.634
And an iced tea.

00:12:40.718 --> 00:12:42.011
I'm getting pretty good at this.

00:12:42.052 --> 00:12:44.054
- Excellent.
- Good job.

00:12:44.138 --> 00:12:45.681
Good for me.

00:12:53.856 --> 00:12:56.400
[mumbling]

00:12:59.069 --> 00:13:01.405
- You okay, Phoebe?
- Yeah. No, I'm just, it's, uh..

00:13:01.489 --> 00:13:04.158
It's not even worth.
It's my bank.

00:13:04.241 --> 00:13:05.409
And what did they do to you?

00:13:05.493 --> 00:13:07.369
It's not,
it's just.. Okay.

00:13:07.411 --> 00:13:08.746
I'm goin' through
my mail, and I open

00:13:08.746 --> 00:13:10.331
up their monthly,
you know, statement--

00:13:10.414 --> 00:13:12.583
- Easy, easy.
- And, yeah..

00:13:13.751 --> 00:13:16.420
And there's $500
extra in my account.

00:13:16.504 --> 00:13:20.090
Oh! Satan's minions
at work again.

00:13:20.341 --> 00:13:23.010
Yes, 'cause now I have to go
down there and deal with them.

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:24.929
What are you talkin' about?
Keep it.

00:13:25.221 --> 00:13:27.348
It's not mine.
I didn't earned it.

00:13:27.431 --> 00:13:29.099
If I kept it,
it would be like stealing.

00:13:29.433 --> 00:13:32.895
Yeah, but if you spent it,
it would be like shopping.

00:13:34.104 --> 00:13:35.439
Okay. Okay.

00:13:35.564 --> 00:13:37.775
Let's say I bought
a really great pair of shoes.

00:13:37.775 --> 00:13:40.277
Do you know what I'd hear
with every step I took?

00:13:40.277 --> 00:13:43.030
Not mine. Not mine. Not mine.

00:13:43.113 --> 00:13:45.950
And even if I was happy,
okay, and, and skipping.

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:48.369
I'd hear, not-not mine.
Not-not mine.

00:13:49.370 --> 00:13:50.955
We're with you. We got it

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:53.958
Okay. I just, I'd never
be able to enjoy it.

00:13:53.958 --> 00:13:56.460
It would be like
this giant karmic debt.

00:13:56.544 --> 00:13:58.128
(Monica)
'Chandler, what are you doin'?'

00:13:58.212 --> 00:14:00.464
Hey, what are you doing?

00:14:03.717 --> 00:14:05.761
- Oh, whoa!
- Oh, gross.

00:14:05.803 --> 00:14:07.388
- What are you doing?
- What is this?

00:14:07.471 --> 00:14:08.889
I'm smoking. I'm smoking
I'm smoking.

00:14:08.973 --> 00:14:09.974
Oh, I can't believe you.

00:14:10.099 --> 00:14:11.976
You've been so good
for three years.

00:14:12.101 --> 00:14:14.478
And this...is my reward.

00:14:15.813 --> 00:14:17.147
Hold on a second, alright.

00:14:17.231 --> 00:14:18.315
Just think about what you went

00:14:18.315 --> 00:14:19.650
through the last time you quit.

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:21.277
Okay, so this time I won't quit.

00:14:21.318 --> 00:14:23.237
- No! Put it down.
- Alright! I'm putting it out.

00:14:23.320 --> 00:14:25.322
I'm putting it out.

00:14:25.406 --> 00:14:28.993
Oh, no! I, uh..
I can't drink this now.

00:14:33.163 --> 00:14:35.416
Alright, I'm gonna go change.
I've got a date.

00:14:35.499 --> 00:14:38.168
Is this Alan again?
How's it goin'?

00:14:38.168 --> 00:14:40.754
It's going pretty good,
you know.

00:14:40.838 --> 00:14:42.423
It's nice and we're having fun.

00:14:42.506 --> 00:14:43.674
So, when do we get
to meet the guy?

00:14:43.799 --> 00:14:46.677
- 'Yeah?'
- Let's see, today's Monday.

00:14:46.802 --> 00:14:48.679
- Never.
- Come on!

00:14:48.679 --> 00:14:50.681
No, no, not after
what happened with Steve.

00:14:50.806 --> 00:14:53.350
What are you talking about?
We love Steve.

00:14:53.475 --> 00:14:55.644
Steve was sexy!

00:14:58.355 --> 00:14:59.690
- Sorry.
- Yeah.

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:01.025
Look, I don't even know
how I feel about him yet.

00:15:01.025 --> 00:15:02.693
Just give me a chance
to figure that out.

00:15:02.818 --> 00:15:05.195
Well, then can we meet him?

00:15:05.279 --> 00:15:07.489
No. Sorry.

00:15:07.781 --> 00:15:09.617
- And lamb chop..
- 'Ooh, lamb chop.'

00:15:09.700 --> 00:15:12.077
How old is that sock?

00:15:13.412 --> 00:15:14.955
If I had a sock on my
hand for thirty years

00:15:15.039 --> 00:15:16.582
it'd be talking too.

00:15:18.792 --> 00:15:20.711
Okay, I think
it's time to change

00:15:20.753 --> 00:15:23.088
somebody's nicotine patch.

00:15:24.965 --> 00:15:28.218
Hey! Where's Joey?

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:31.805
Joey ate my last stick
of gum, so I killed him.

00:15:32.973 --> 00:15:35.267
Do you think that was wrong?

00:15:36.727 --> 00:15:38.312
I think he's across the hall.

00:15:38.395 --> 00:15:39.647
Thanks.

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:42.066
There you go.

00:15:42.107 --> 00:15:45.444
Ooh, I'm alive
with pleasure now.

00:15:45.486 --> 00:15:48.155
Hey, Pheebs, you gonna have
the rest of that Pop-Tart?

00:15:48.238 --> 00:15:50.282
Pheebs?

00:15:50.324 --> 00:15:53.118
Does anyone want
the rest of this Pop-Tart?

00:15:54.828 --> 00:15:57.331
Hey, I might.

00:15:57.456 --> 00:15:59.124
Sorry.

00:15:59.166 --> 00:16:01.001
You know, those stupid
soda people gave me

00:16:01.126 --> 00:16:02.836
seven thousand
dollars for the thumb.

00:16:02.962 --> 00:16:04.838
- Oh, my God!
- Seven thousand dollars?

00:16:04.964 --> 00:16:07.841
And on my way over here,
I stepped in gum.

00:16:09.093 --> 00:16:11.303
What is up with the universe?

00:16:11.345 --> 00:16:12.930
- What's goin' on?
- Nothing.

00:16:12.972 --> 00:16:14.139
I just think it's nice when

00:16:14.181 --> 00:16:15.641
we're all here together.

00:16:15.683 --> 00:16:16.976
