and the six of clubs.

01:48:16.990 --> 01:48:18.825
No, Pheebs,
you can't do--

01:48:18.825 --> 01:48:20.285
Oh, wait, I have the ten of
spades. Here, you want it?

01:48:20.285 --> 01:48:21.536
No, no.

01:48:23.455 --> 01:48:25.749
Uh, no, see,
you-you can't do that.

01:48:25.832 --> 01:48:27.209
Oh, no, no, no,
that's okay.

01:48:27.250 --> 01:48:28.627
I don't need them.
I'm going for fours.

01:48:28.710 --> 01:48:31.254
Oh, you're..

01:48:35.550 --> 01:48:36.676
Alright, here we go.

01:48:36.968 --> 01:48:39.554
We got salmon roulettes
and assorted crudites.

01:48:39.971 --> 01:48:41.973
Whoa, whoa, whoa, Monica,
what are you doin'?

01:48:42.307 --> 01:48:44.226
This is a poker game,
you can't serve food

01:48:44.267 --> 01:48:45.810
with more than
one syllable.

01:48:46.311 --> 01:48:49.648
It's gotta be like
chips, or dip, or pretz.

01:48:52.567 --> 01:48:53.860
Okay, so at this point,
the dealer--

01:48:53.902 --> 01:48:55.612
Alright, you know, we got it.
Let's play for real, alright?

01:48:55.820 --> 01:48:58.532
- High stakes, big bucks.
- Alright, now, you sure?

01:48:58.615 --> 01:48:59.991
Pheebe just threw
away two jacks

01:48:59.991 --> 01:49:01.993
because they didn't
look happy.

01:49:06.581 --> 01:49:09.042
But, I'm ready,
so just deal.

01:49:09.501 --> 01:49:11.253
Okay. Alright, last-minute
lesson, last-minute lesson.

01:49:11.419 --> 01:49:14.005
Joey, three..

01:49:14.381 --> 01:49:15.215
...eight.

01:49:16.049 --> 01:49:18.385
Eight, three.
Alright. Very good.

01:49:23.306 --> 01:49:25.183
Dammit! Dammit! Dammit!

01:49:25.976 --> 01:49:27.894
I see. So then,
you were lying.

01:49:28.353 --> 01:49:28.853
About what?

01:49:29.229 --> 01:49:30.814
About how good
your cards were.

01:49:31.273 --> 01:49:32.190
I was bluffing.

01:49:32.691 --> 01:49:35.443
Uh-huh. And what is bluffing?

01:49:37.612 --> 01:49:40.115
Is it not another word
for lying?

01:49:41.116 --> 01:49:43.243
Okay, sorry to
break up this party

01:49:43.285 --> 01:49:45.912
but, I've got resumes to
fax before lunch tomorrow.

01:49:46.621 --> 01:49:47.998
Rach, Rach,
we gotta settle.

01:49:48.415 --> 01:49:49.249
Settle what?

01:49:50.750 --> 01:49:53.336
The Jamestown colony
of Virginia.

01:49:55.046 --> 01:49:57.257
You see King George
is giving us the land, so..

01:50:00.677 --> 01:50:02.554
The game, Rachel.
The game.

01:50:02.762 --> 01:50:03.930
You owe us money
for the game.

01:50:04.097 --> 01:50:05.181
Oh. Right.

01:50:05.307 --> 01:50:07.142
You know, what, you guys,
it's their first time.

01:50:07.183 --> 01:50:09.060
Why don't we just
forget about the money.

01:50:09.185 --> 01:50:10.687
Hell, no,
we'll pay!

01:50:11.605 --> 01:50:14.107
Monica, I had
another answer all ready.

01:50:16.484 --> 01:50:18.903
And you know what?
We want a rematch.

01:50:19.321 --> 01:50:20.405
Well, that's
fine with me.

01:50:20.947 --> 01:50:22.657
Could use the money.

01:50:23.908 --> 01:50:25.785
So basically,
you get your ya-yas

01:50:25.869 --> 01:50:28.163
by taking money
from all of your friends.

01:50:28.913 --> 01:50:29.414
Yeah.

01:50:29.748 --> 01:50:32.125
Yes, and I get my ya-yas
from IKEA.

01:50:34.377 --> 01:50:35.795
You have to put them
together yourself

01:50:35.795 --> 01:50:37.464
but they cost
a little less.

01:50:39.090 --> 01:50:40.467
Look, Rach,
this is poker.

01:50:40.717 --> 01:50:42.218
I play to win, alright?

01:50:42.302 --> 01:50:44.638
In order for me to win,
other people have to lose.

01:50:44.929 --> 01:50:46.306
So, if you're gonna
play poker with me

01:50:46.306 --> 01:50:48.350
don't expect me
to be a nice guy.

01:50:48.600 --> 01:50:50.560
Okay, 'cause once
those cards are dealt..

01:51:00.654 --> 01:51:01.696
Yeah?

01:51:05.659 --> 01:51:07.285
I'm not a nice guy.

01:51:10.747 --> 01:51:13.500
Boy, you really can't
stand to lose, can you?

01:51:14.042 --> 01:51:15.251
Your whole face
is getting red.

01:51:15.335 --> 01:51:18.421
The little vein's
popping outta your temple

01:51:19.547 --> 01:51:21.841
Plus, that shirt doesn't
really match those pants.

01:51:26.763 --> 01:51:27.931
First of all, I'm not losing, I-

01:51:28.348 --> 01:51:29.599
[phone ringing]
- Oh, you're definitely losing..
- Let's not talk about losing--

01:51:30.100 --> 01:51:31.434
Hello. Rachel Green.

01:51:31.434 --> 01:51:32.769
[imitating]
Me-me-me.

01:51:34.104 --> 01:51:36.523
Excuse me. It's about the job..

01:51:37.565 --> 01:51:39.442
Barbara, hi.
How are you?

01:51:42.237 --> 01:51:42.779
Uh-huh.

01:51:44.698 --> 01:51:45.782
No, I understand.

01:51:47.033 --> 01:51:49.869
Yeah, oh, well,
come on, no, I'm fine.

01:51:50.370 --> 01:51:51.287
Don't be silly.

01:51:52.122 --> 01:51:56.042
Yeah, but, you know,
if anything else opens up..

01:51:56.209 --> 01:51:57.585
please-
hello?

01:51:59.546 --> 01:52:00.088
Hello?

01:52:01.881 --> 01:52:03.216
[scoffs]

01:52:09.723 --> 01:52:10.932
Hmm.

01:52:16.563 --> 01:52:17.772
Sorry, Rach.

01:52:17.939 --> 01:52:19.899
Yeah, you know, there's
gonna be lots of other stuff.

01:52:20.233 --> 01:52:22.402
Yeah. Okay.

01:52:23.987 --> 01:52:24.821
Where were we?

01:52:25.405 --> 01:52:27.490
Oh. Okay. Five-card draw.

01:52:28.074 --> 01:52:30.076
Uh...jacks or better.

01:52:30.827 --> 01:52:32.412
Nothing wild.
Everybody ante.

01:52:33.246 --> 01:52:35.290
Look, Rach, we don't
have to do this.

01:52:36.166 --> 01:52:37.083
Yes, we do.

01:52:40.253 --> 01:52:42.255
- Alright, check.
- Check.

01:52:42.797 --> 01:52:44.257
I'm in for 50 cents.

01:52:44.841 --> 01:52:46.760
- Call.
- I'm in.

01:52:48.178 --> 01:52:50.263
I see your 50 cents..

01:52:51.181 --> 01:52:54.601
...and I raise you...$5.

01:52:55.435 --> 01:52:57.687
I thought it was
a 50-cent limit.

01:52:57.812 --> 01:52:59.481
Well, I just lost a job
and I'd like to raise

01:52:59.481 --> 01:53:00.940
the bet five bucks.

01:53:01.107 --> 01:53:03.777
Does anybody have
a problem with that?

01:53:04.277 --> 01:53:06.946
[indistinct chatter]

01:53:10.325 --> 01:53:11.326
Loser?

01:53:19.834 --> 01:53:20.794
No, I fold.

01:53:21.294 --> 01:53:23.630
What do you mean you fo?
Hey, come on, what is this?

01:53:23.630 --> 01:53:28.301
I thought that "once the cards
are dealt, I'm not a nice guy"

01:53:28.510 --> 01:53:30.512
I mean what, were you
just full of it?

01:53:44.484 --> 01:53:44.984
I'm in.

01:53:46.319 --> 01:53:47.237
How many you want?

01:53:47.570 --> 01:53:48.071
One.

01:53:49.989 --> 01:53:51.324
Dealer takes two.

01:53:52.075 --> 01:53:55.161
- 'What do you bet?'
- I bet $2.

01:53:56.704 --> 01:53:59.332
Okay, see your two..

01:53:59.833 --> 01:54:02.377
...and I raise you..

01:54:03.837 --> 01:54:04.587
...twenty.

01:54:04.587 --> 01:54:05.338
Wha..

01:54:10.510 --> 01:54:12.846
I'll see your 20..

01:54:13.346 --> 01:54:15.849
...raise you 25.

01:54:21.020 --> 01:54:22.522
See your 25..

01:54:23.398 --> 01:54:25.191
...and, uh, Monica,
get my purse.

01:54:30.697 --> 01:54:32.407
Rachel, there's
nothing in it.

01:54:34.200 --> 01:54:36.202
Okay, then get me your purse.

01:54:40.415 --> 01:54:43.418
Okay...here you go.
Good luck.

01:54:43.793 --> 01:54:44.419
Thank you.

01:54:45.253 --> 01:54:49.132
I saw your 25,
and I raise you..

01:54:49.132 --> 01:54:49.799
...seven.

01:54:51.926 --> 01:54:53.303
-teen.

01:55:01.436 --> 01:55:02.812
Joey, I'm a little shy.

01:55:04.272 --> 01:55:07.609
That's okay, Ross.
You can ask me.

01:55:13.489 --> 01:55:15.617
- What do you need?
What do you need?
- Fifteen.

01:55:15.742 --> 01:55:17.410
- Here's ten.
- Here, I got five. I got five.

01:55:17.785 --> 01:55:20.246
- Thank you.
- Good luck.

01:55:20.914 --> 01:55:23.666
Okay, I am calling your seventen

01:55:24.125 --> 01:55:26.002
What do you got?

01:55:26.461 --> 01:55:29.005
[dramatic music]

01:55:36.262 --> 01:55:37.305
Full house.

01:55:46.314 --> 01:55:46.940
You got me.

01:55:47.357 --> 01:55:49.692
- Oh!
- Oh!

01:55:50.318 --> 01:55:51.611
♪ Da da da da da-da

01:55:52.195 --> 01:55:53.780
♪ Da da da da da-da

01:55:54.030 --> 01:55:55.281
Oh..

01:55:55.531 --> 01:55:57.158
Oh!

01:55:59.118 --> 01:56:00.703
That's alright, you know,
that's a tough hand to beat.

01:56:00.787 --> 01:56:02.288
I thought we had them!

01:56:02.288 --> 01:56:03.831
When you don't have the cards,
you don't have the cards.

01:56:04.374 --> 01:56:04.832
But, uh...

01:56:06.000 --> 01:56:07.502
Look how happy she is.

01:56:14.884 --> 01:56:15.969
How could you lose him?

01:56:16.052 --> 01:56:17.095
I don't know,
I don't know.

01:56:17.220 --> 01:56:18.262
We were watching TV

01:56:18.262 --> 01:56:19.889
and then he pooped
in Monica's shoe..

01:56:20.098 --> 01:56:22.725
Wait. He pooped
in my shoe?

01:56:23.434 --> 01:56:25.061
- Which one?
- I don't know.

01:56:25.561 --> 01:56:28.272
- The left one.
- Which ones?

01:56:28.439 --> 01:56:30.441
Oh, oh, those little
clunky Amish things

01:56:30.441 --> 01:56:31.818
you think go
with everything.

01:56:33.903 --> 01:56:35.238
-Hey.
- Hi.

01:56:35.571 --> 01:56:36.406
Whoa. Oh.

01:56:36.656 --> 01:56:38.783
Why is the air in
here so negative?

01:56:40.410 --> 01:56:43.496
- Rachel lost Marcel.
- Oh, no! How?

01:56:43.621 --> 01:56:46.124
- He-he pooped in my shoe.
- Which one?

01:56:46.124 --> 01:56:48.251
Those cute little black
ones I wear all the tim.e

01:56:48.626 --> 01:56:50.003
No. Which one?

01:56:51.087 --> 01:56:52.171
The right or left?

01:56:53.756 --> 01:56:55.174
'Cause the left
one is lucky.

01:56:55.967 --> 01:56:57.760
Come on, you guys, what are we
gonna do? What are we gonna do?

01:56:57.802 --> 01:56:59.637
Alright, alright, alright...
You're a monkey.

01:57:00.013 --> 01:57:01.597
You're loose in the city.

01:57:02.015 --> 01:57:02.974
Where do you go?

01:57:04.267 --> 01:57:06.769
Okay, it's his first time out,
so he's probably gonna wanna do

01:57:06.769 --> 01:57:08.312
some of the touristy things.

01:57:11.149 --> 01:57:14.819
I'll go to Cats. You go
to the Russian Tea Room.

01:57:15.528 --> 01:57:18.322
Oh, my God! Come on, you guys!

01:57:18.364 --> 01:57:20.783
He's gonna be home any minute!
He's gonna kill me!

01:57:20.867 --> 01:57:22.201
Okay, we'll start
with the building.

01:57:22.368 --> 01:57:23.786
You guys take the first
and second floor.

01:57:23.786 --> 01:57:25.121
Phoebe and I will
take third and fourth.

01:57:25.496 --> 01:57:27.123
W-w-what am I gonna do?
What am I gonna do?

01:57:27.290 --> 01:57:30.126
Okay, you stay here,
and just wait by the phone..

01:57:30.126 --> 01:57:32.503
Spray Lysol in my shoe
and wait for Ross to kill you.

01:57:33.796 --> 01:57:35.673
Does anybody wanna trade? Oh..

01:57:36.215 --> 01:57:38.801
[instrumental music]

01:57:39.135 --> 01:57:39.677
Come on.

01:57:39.844 --> 01:57:40.970
[knocks on door]

01:57:43.639 --> 01:57:44.474
What do you want?

01:57:45.141 --> 01:57:46.726
Mr. Heckles, our-our-our
friend lost a monkey.

01:57:46.851 --> 01:57:47.810
Have you seen it?

01:57:48.644 --> 01:57:50.146
I left a Belgian
waffle out here.

01:57:50.146 --> 01:57:52.315
- Did you take it?
- No!

01:57:52.648 --> 01:57:54.984
Why would you leave your
Belgian waffle in the hall?

01:57:55.401 --> 01:57:56.652
I wasn't ready for it.

01:57:57.236 --> 01:57:57.820
The monkey..

01:57:57.862 --> 01:57:59.655
Have you seen a monkey?

01:58:00.239 --> 01:58:02.325
Saw Regis Philbin once.

01:58:03.034 --> 01:58:04.577
Okay, thank you,
Mr. Heckles.

01:58:06.037 --> 01:58:07.830
You owe me a waffle.

01:58:08.831 --> 01:58:11.417
Okay, he's a, he's
a black capuchin monkey

01:58:11.417 --> 01:58:12.752
with a white face

01:58:13.002 --> 01:58:17.340
with-with Russian dressing
and pickles on the side.

01:58:17.715 --> 01:58:19.550
Okay. Thanks.

01:58:20.510 --> 01:58:21.344
- Hi.
- Hey.

01:58:21.511 --> 01:58:22.762
How did, uh,
how did it go today?

01:58:22.845 --> 01:58:24.097
- Oh, great!
- Yeah?

01:58:24.097 --> 01:58:25.765
It went great.
Really great.

01:58:25.765 --> 01:58:27.767
- Hey, is that wine?
- Yeah, yeah.

01:58:27.850 --> 01:58:29.894
- Oh.
- You, uh, you want some?

01:58:29.894 --> 01:58:31.229
Oh, I would love some.

01:58:32.021 --> 01:58:33.189
But you know what?
You know what?

01:58:33.189 --> 01:58:34.690
Let's not drink it here.

01:58:34.690 --> 01:58:36.109
I'm feeling kind of crazy.

01:58:36.109 --> 01:58:37.401
You wanna go to Newark?

01:58:40.530 --> 01:58:43.407
Uh, okay. Yeah, uh,
we could do that.

01:58:43.407 --> 01:58:45.409
But before we head off
to the murder capital

01:58:45.409 --> 01:58:46.702
of the Northeast..

01:58:47.870 --> 01:58:50.957
...I was, uh.. Kind of wanted to
to run something by you.

01:58:51.374 --> 01:58:53.751
You know how we were, uh,
you know, talking before

01:58:53.751 --> 01:58:57.380
about, uh, relationships
and stuff, well..

01:58:57.380 --> 01:58:59.048
Oh, God, Ross,
I cannot do this.

01:58:59.215 --> 01:59:00.383
Okay, quick
and painful.

01:59:10.143 --> 01:59:12.562
Oh, God.
Okay, alright.

01:59:12.562 --> 01:59:13.980
Alright, okay.

01:59:14.730 --> 01:59:16.607
Ross, please
don't hate me.

01:59:17.150 --> 01:59:18.276
Oh, why? What? What?

01:59:18.276 --> 01:59:19.235
[chuckles]

01:59:20.069 --> 01:59:22.405
Uh, you know Marcel?

01:59:23.739 --> 01:59:24.740
Yeah?

01:59:24.740 --> 01:59:27.743
Well, ahem,
I, I kind of..

01:59:28.286 --> 01:59:30.079
...I kind of lost him.

01:59:30.246 --> 01:59:31.664
[indistinct]

01:59:31.998 --> 01:59:34.667
[car horn honking]

01:59:41.924 --> 01:59:43.801
- 'Marcel?'
- 'Marcel?'

01:59:44.093 --> 01:59:45.344
Marcel?

01:59:46.262 --> 01:59:47.513
(both)
Marcel?

01:59:48.139 --> 01:59:49.223
- Oh, my God!
- What?

01:59:49.390 --> 01:59:51.309
Something just brushed up
against my right leg.

01:59:51.392 --> 01:59:52.643
- What is it?
- Oh.

01:59:53.352 --> 01:59:55.521
Oh, it's okay.
It was just my left leg.

01:59:56.731 --> 01:59:57.440
[screeching]

01:59:58.232 --> 02:00:00.109
- 'Look, Phoebe!'
- Oh, yeah. Oh, Marcel.

02:00:00.276 --> 02:00:02.403
Come here. Oh,
come here, Marcel.

02:00:02.403 --> 02:00:03.863
Step aside, ladies.

02:00:05.114 --> 02:00:06.240
Oh, what are you gonna do?

02:00:06.407 --> 02:00:08.075
Just a small tranquilizer.

02:00:08.534 --> 02:00:11.579
[dramatic music]

02:00:23.883 --> 02:00:25.259
(Monica)
'Run, Marcel! Run!'

02:00:25.426 --> 02:00:26.761
- Run, Marcel!
- Damn!

02:00:27.720 --> 02:00:30.681
- Are you okay?
- Uh, yeah, I think so.

02:00:30.806 --> 02:00:31.807
I just..

02:00:31.891 --> 02:00:33.226
Oh.

02:00:34.894 --> 02:00:35.895
Huh..

02:00:36.604 --> 02:00:39.232
- Whoa.
-Oh.

02:00:39.607 --> 02:00:40.650
Oh, gosh.

02:00:45.863 --> 02:00:47.156
[screeching]

02:00:49.116 --> 02:00:50.618
- 'Marcel?'
- 'Marcel?'

02:00:50.660 --> 02:00:52.912
Marcel? This is ridiculous!

02:00:52.912 --> 02:00:53.996
We've been all over
the neighborhood.

02:00:54.121 --> 02:00:55.873
He's gone. He's-he's just gone!

02:00:55.873 --> 02:00:57.083
- Ross, you don't know that.
- Oh, come on.

02:00:57.917 --> 02:01:00.544
It's cold. It's dark.
He doesn't know the village!

02:01:00.795 --> 02:01:00.962
Oh..

02:01:01.837 --> 02:01:02.964
And now I have
a broken foot. Oh, my.

02:01:03.798 --> 02:01:06.425
I have no monkey
and a broken foot.

02:01:06.968 --> 02:01:09.095
- Thank you very much.
- Ross, you know?

02:01:09.095 --> 02:01:11.305
I've said I'm sorry
like a million times.

02:01:11.347 --> 02:01:13.099
What do you want me to ?
Huh? What do you wanna..

02:01:13.099 --> 02:01:14.976
You want to break my fo?
Is that it? Okay, here.

02:01:14.976 --> 02:01:15.810
I'm gonna break my foot.
Right now, there.

02:01:16.310 --> 02:01:18.646
Ow! Oh! Oh, God!

02:01:18.688 --> 02:01:21.190
Oh, my God. There,
are you happy now?

02:01:21.232 --> 02:01:23.359
Yeah, yeah, you know, now
that you kicked the sign

02:01:23.359 --> 02:01:27.613
hey! What? I don't
miss Marcel anymore.

02:01:30.074 --> 02:01:32.326
You know, it is not like
I did this on purpose.

02:01:32.326 --> 02:01:34.996
No, no, no, this is
just vintage Rachel.

02:01:35.121 --> 02:01:38.040
I mean, things just
sort of happen around you.

02:01:38.040 --> 02:01:40.167
I mean, you're
off in Rachel Land

02:01:40.167 --> 02:01:41.502
doing your Rachel thing

02:01:41.502 --> 02:01:44.338
totally oblivious
to people's monkeys

02:01:44.338 --> 02:01:46.048
or to people's
feelings and..

02:01:46.048 --> 02:01:47.717
- Ross?
- I don't even wanna hear it.

02:01:47.883 --> 02:01:49.093
- No, you're always--
- Ross..

02:01:49.093 --> 02:01:50.511
- Oh, forget it, okay?
- Ross!

02:01:50.511 --> 02:01:52.263
What? What? What?

02:01:55.349 --> 02:01:57.435
- Hey!
- Hey! Banana man! Wait..

02:01:57.977 --> 02:02:01.105
[instrumental music]

02:02:01.814 --> 02:02:03.274
[knocking on door]

02:02:03.858 --> 02:02:04.942
Oh, this is so intense.

