02:23:44.532 --> 02:23:47.660
Except for um...
no, everyone.

02:23:50.830 --> 02:23:51.789
What are you talking about?

02:23:52.373 --> 02:23:55.627
Don't feel bad. You know,
they used to like you a alot.

02:23:56.544 --> 02:23:58.212
But, then you got promoted,
and you know

02:23:58.212 --> 02:24:00.381
now you're all
like Mr. Boss man.

02:24:00.465 --> 02:24:03.384
You know, Mr. Bing. Mr..
Boss man Bing.

02:24:06.012 --> 02:24:06.804
I can't believe it.

02:24:07.347 --> 02:24:09.307
Yeah, yeah.
They even do you.

02:24:11.059 --> 02:24:12.226
They "do" me?

02:24:12.977 --> 02:24:14.562
You know like, um,
okay, um

02:24:15.480 --> 02:24:17.231
"Could that report
be any later."

02:24:17.565 --> 02:24:19.692
[laughing]

02:24:23.738 --> 02:24:24.405
I don't sound like that.

02:24:24.906 --> 02:24:27.241
- Oh. Oh, Chandler.
- Yeah, you do.

02:24:28.076 --> 02:24:31.037
"The hills are alive
with the sound..

02:24:31.579 --> 02:24:33.373
...of music."

02:24:39.003 --> 02:24:39.921
"My scone!"

02:24:40.004 --> 02:24:41.756
Both: "My scone!"

02:24:43.758 --> 02:24:46.219
Okay. I don't sound like.
That is so not true.

02:24:46.594 --> 02:24:48.429
[laughing]

02:24:49.347 --> 02:24:52.183
That is so not
...that is so not...that..

02:24:52.600 --> 02:24:53.851
Oh, shut up!

02:24:58.272 --> 02:25:00.066
And I think last night
was great, you know

02:25:00.066 --> 02:25:02.068
the karaoke thing. Tracy
and I doing Ebony and Ivory?

02:25:02.568 --> 02:25:03.778
